<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>18 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta), Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>14 - Abel Balbo (Roma)</p>
<p>13 - Roberto Mancini</p>
<p>12 - Marcelo Otero (Vicenza), Sandro Tovalieri (Cagliari)</p>
<p>11 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Youri Djorkaeff (Inter),</p>
<p>Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna), Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>10 - Enrico Chiesa (Parma), George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p>9 - Filippo Maniero (Verona), Marco Negri (Perugia), Paolo</p>
<p>Poggi (Udinese)</p>
<p>8 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Marco Amoroso and Oliver</p>
<p>Bierhoff (both Udinese), Alessandro Del Piero and Michele</p>
<p>Padovano (both Juventus), Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>7 - Roberto Muzzi (Cagliari), Anselmo Robbiati (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>6 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria),</p>
<p>Hernan Crespo (Parma), Kennet Andersson (Bologna), Roberto</p>
<p>Murgita (Vicenza), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>5 - Marco Branca and Maurizio Ganz (Inter), Nicola Caccia,</p>
<p>Andre Cruz and Fabio Pecchia (all Napoli), Giampiero Maini</p>
<p>(Vicenza), Domenico Morfeo (Atalanta), Pierluigi Orlandini</p>
<p>(Verona), Igor Simutenkov (Reggiana), Christian Vieri (Juventus)</p>
